      "Reverse-curve gutter guards, sometimes called surface-tension or 'helmet' style guards, work on a different principle than every other guard on this list: rather than filtering debris through a mesh or foam barrier, the solid cover uses the physical property of water clinging to a curved surface to pull rainwater around the curve and into the gutter, while heavier leaves and debris simply can't make the turn and slide off the front edge to the ground. When installed correctly, this means there's no mesh to clog and nothing inside the gutter that ever needs cleaning or replacing — a genuine long-term advantage over any filter-based system. The catch, and it's a significant one, is that the system's effectiveness depends heavily on matching the guard's angle to your specific roof pitch; in our testing, a unit installed at the wrong angle for a low-slope roof section let a noticeable amount of water overshoot the gutter during a simulated heavy downpour rather than curving in as intended. Properly installed on a compatible roof pitch, it performed impressively, handling sustained heavy rain without any overflow while keeping large leaves out entirely. Fine debris like helicopter seeds and small twigs occasionally found their way through the narrow front opening, so it's not a total exclusion system, but for homes with primarily large-leaf trees and a standard roof pitch, it's a genuinely low-maintenance long-term option.",
  },
  {
    id: "raptor-round-gutter-guards",
    name: "Raptor Round Gutter Guards",
    category: "Micro-Mesh for Round/Half-Round Gutters",
    badge: "Best for Round Gutters",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 2100,
    pros: [
      "Purpose-built for half-round gutter profiles that most mainstream guards don't fit properly",
      "Same stainless micro-mesh material and effectiveness as Raptor's standard K-style product",
      "Clip-on design specifically engineered for the curved lip of round gutters",
      "Preserves the visual profile of half-round gutters, common on historic and higher-end homes",
      "Bulk roll format works for whole-house half-round gutter systems",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Meaningfully more expensive than standard K-style guards due to the specialized profile",
      "Fewer stockists carry it compared to standard gutter guard products, so ordering ahead matters",
