          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Micro-mesh gutter guards, like the Raptor Gutter Guards or Gutter Glove Ultra, offer the best overall protection because they block nearly all debris — leaves, pine needles, and shingle grit — while still allowing strong water flow. Reverse-curve guards are a strong low-maintenance alternative for homes with mostly large leaves and a compatible roof pitch.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do gutter guards really work?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, when the right type is matched to your property's debris and correctly installed. Micro-mesh guards block the vast majority of leaves, needles, and debris while passing water through effectively. No gutter guard eliminates maintenance entirely, but a well-chosen system reduces cleaning from twice a year to roughly once a year or less.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I install gutter guards myself?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. Foam and brush inserts require no tools and can be installed by simply cutting to length and pressing into the gutter. Snap-on mesh and reverse-curve systems require basic tools, a ladder, and roughly a weekend for an average single-story home, but are within reach of most reasonably handy DIYers.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do gutter guards stop pine needles?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Standard micro-mesh handles most pine needles, but fine, tightly-woven mesh products like Gutter Glove Ultra or foam inserts like GutterStuff are specifically better suited to needle-heavy properties, since standard mesh can occasionally let the thinnest needles through as openings wear slightly larger over time.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do gutter guards eliminate the need to clean gutters?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. Gutter guards significantly reduce how often you need to clean gutters, but fine debris like roof grit, seeds, and dust can still accumulate on top of most guards over time and benefits from an annual check. Foam and brush inserts especially still need periodic surface debris removal.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much do gutter guards cost to install?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "DIY gutter guard materials typically cost $3-10 per linear foot depending on the type, with foam and brush inserts at the low end and premium stainless micro-mesh at the high end. For an average home with 150-200 feet of gutter, DIY material costs usually run $500-1,500. Professional installation adds significantly more, often $7-20 per linear foot including labor.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "All Metal Brake" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
      review: {
        "@type": "Review",
        reviewBody: product.bottomLine,
        author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
        publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "All Metal Brake" },
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home & Roofing",
    tags: [
      "gutter guards",
      "micro mesh gutter guard",
      "leaf guard",
      "gutter protection",
      "roof and gutter maintenance",
      "home improvement",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
